---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout title="About | William Schibler">

  <section class="page-hero info-page-hero">
    <div class="page-container">
      <p class="eyebrow">About</p>
      <h1>Engineering through Analysis, Design, and Testing.</h1>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section two-column professional-bio">

    <div class="bio-media">

      <div class="bio-photo-frame">
        <img
          src="/images/headshot.jpg"
          alt="Professional portrait of William Schibler"
        />
      </div>
      <p class="bio-name">William T. Schibler</p>
    </div>

    <div class="bio-copy">
      <h2>My Engineering Story</h2>

      <p>
        I chose to study mechanical and aerospace engineering because I wanted a
        broad but rigorous technical foundation for my career. Aerospace systems
        bring together structures, fluids, propulsion, controls, electronics,
        manufacturing, and many other disciplines, making systems-level thinking
        essential. I believe that understanding how these disciplines interact
        makes an engineer more effective when collaborating across disciplines and
        identifying project design constraints. For that reason, I have always
        wanted my engineering education to extend beyond the confines of a single
        discipline.
      </p>

      <p>
        I am capable of adapting to different types of engineering work, but I
        particularly enjoy projects that are hands-on and allow me to take
        ownership of the creative process, whether that be with a team or by
        myself. Further, I also appreciate roles that foster systems-level
        thinking and require interdisciplinary collaboration; they help shape the
        mind to envision and understand projects that operate on a larger scale.
      </p>

      <p>
        Ultimately, I want to apply my engineering skills to meaningful projects
        that help people. Whether that be working on satellites to collect global
        data, improving combustion systems for efficiency, optimizing rockets for
        flight, or anything else I do in the future, I want my endeavors to serve
        a greater purpose than just myself.
      </p>
    </div>

  </section>

  <section class="section section-border">
    <div class="section-heading">
      <p class="eyebrow">Education</p>
    </div>

    <div class="education">
      <div class="education-logo">
        <img
          src="/images/northeastern-monogram.png"
          alt="Northeastern University monogram"
        />
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2>Northeastern University</h2>
        <h3>B.S. Mechanical Engineering</h3>
        <p>Aerospace Engineering minor · Expected May 2028</p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <strong>GPA: 3.93</strong>
        <p><strong>Extracurriculars:</strong> Tau Beta Pi · ExClub President</p>
        <p><strong>Awards:</strong> Dean’s List · ASME Student of the Week</p>
      </div>
    </div>

 
  </section>

  <section class="section">
  <div class="section-heading engineering-interests-heading">
    <p class="eyebrow">Engineering Interests</p>
  </div>

  <div class="interest-grid">

    <details class="capability-card interest-card" name="engineering-interest">
      <summary class="interest-summary">
        <div class="capability-card-heading">
          <div class="capability-icon interest-icon" aria-hidden="true">
            <svg
              viewBox="0 0 24 24"
              fill="none"
              stroke="currentColor"
              stroke-width="1.6"
              stroke-linecap="round"
              stroke-linejoin="round"
            >
              <path d="M4.5 16.5c-1.5 1.26-2 5-2 5s3.74-.5 5-2c.71-.84.7-2.13-.09-2.91a2.18 2.18 0 0 0-2.91-.09Z" />
              <path d="m12 15-3-3a22 22 0 0 1 2-3.95A12.87 12.87 0 0 1 22 2c0 2.72-.78 7.5-6.05 11A22.35 22.35 0 0 1 12 15Z" />
              <path d="M9 12H4s.55-3.03 2-4c1.62-1.08 5 0 5 0" />
              <path d="M12 15v5s3.03-.55 4-2c1.08-1.62 0-5 0-5" />
              <circle cx="16" cy="8" r="1" />
            </svg>
          </div>

          <h3>Aerospace Propulsion</h3>
        </div>

        <p class="interest-teaser">
          Systems-level propulsion engineering integrating flow, chemistry,
          cryogenics, and spacecraft performance.
        </p>

        <span class="interest-chevron" aria-hidden="true"></span>
      </summary>

      <div class="interest-expanded">
        <p>
          Optimized propulsion for space travel requires an understanding of flow
          system design/analysis, chemistry, and cryogenics as well as how the
          propulsion system interacts with the overall spacecraft.
          In my career, I aim
          to develop a wide range of skills that allow me to better understand how
          subsystems interact and how those interactions affect propulsion
          performance.
        </p>
      </div>
    </details>


    <details class="capability-card interest-card" name="engineering-interest">
      <summary class="interest-summary">
        <div class="capability-card-heading">
          <div class="capability-icon interest-icon" aria-hidden="true">
            <svg
              viewBox="0 0 24 24"
              fill="none"
              stroke="currentColor"
              stroke-width="1.6"
              stroke-linecap="round"
              stroke-linejoin="round"
            >
              <circle cx="12" cy="12" r="3" />
              <path d="M19.4 15a1.7 1.7 0 0 0 .3 1.9l.1.1-2.8 2.8-.1-.1a1.7 1.7 0 0 0-1.9-.3 1.7 1.7 0 0 0-1 1.6v.2h-4V21a1.7 1.7 0 0 0-1-1.6 1.7 1.7 0 0 0-1.9.3l-.1.1L4.2 17l.1-.1a1.7 1.7 0 0 0 .3-1.9A1.7 1.7 0 0 0 3 14H2.8v-4H3a1.7 1.7 0 0 0 1.6-1 1.7 1.7 0 0 0-.3-1.9L4.2 7 7 4.2l.1.1A1.7 1.7 0 0 0 9 4.6 1.7 1.7 0 0 0 10 3v-.2h4V3a1.7 1.7 0 0 0 1 1.6 1.7 1.7 0 0 0 1.9-.3l.1-.1L19.8 7l-.1.1a1.7 1.7 0 0 0-.3 1.9 1.7 1.7 0 0 0 1.6 1h.2v4H21a1.7 1.7 0 0 0-1.6 1Z" />
            </svg>
          </div>

          <h3>Fluid Systems and Turbomachinery</h3>
        </div>

        <p class="interest-teaser">
          How geometry and component design shape fluid behavior, reliability,
          and system performance.
        </p>

        <span class="interest-chevron" aria-hidden="true"></span>
      </summary>

      <div class="interest-expanded">
        <p>
          Understanding how fluid properties change as they move through a system,
          and how geometry and component design influence those changes, is
          essential to effective fluid-system and turbomachinery design. These
          systems must operate reliably, efficiently, and repeatably, in varying
          conditions. I enjoy understanding how geometry and design decisions in
          machinery allow engineers to create the desired outlet conditions in a
          system.
        </p>
      </div>
    </details>


    <details class="capability-card interest-card" name="engineering-interest">
      <summary class="interest-summary">
        <div class="capability-card-heading">
          <div class="capability-icon interest-icon" aria-hidden="true">
            <svg
              viewBox="0 0 24 24"
              fill="none"
              stroke="currentColor"
              stroke-width="1.8"
              stroke-linecap="round"
              stroke-linejoin="round"
            >
              <path d="M15.5 3.5 20.5 8.5 8.5 20.5 3.5 15.5 15.5 3.5Z" />
              <path d="m13.5 5.5 2 2" />
              <path d="m11.5 7.5 1.5 1.5" />
              <path d="m9.5 9.5 2 2" />
              <path d="m7.5 11.5 1.5 1.5" />
            </svg>
          </div>

          <h3>Design, Manufacturing,<br />and Testing</h3>
        </div>

        <p class="interest-teaser">
          Turning concepts into physical prototypes through hands-on design,
          manufacturing, testing, and iteration.
        </p>

        <span class="interest-chevron" aria-hidden="true"></span>
      </summary>

      <div class="interest-expanded">
        <p>
          Being able to turn a concept into a physical, testable prototype is an
          invaluable skill in engineering. It allows creative engineers to test
          out and iterate their designs and ideas. I always seek hands-on work and
          am cultivating the skills necessary to carry a prototype through the
          full process from design and manufacturing to testing and iteration.
        </p>
      </div>
    </details>

  </div>
</section>

  <section class="section section-border">
    <div class="section-heading leadership-service-heading">
      <p class="eyebrow">Leadership and Service</p>
    </div>

    <div class="leadership-list">

      <article class="leadership-card leadership-card--makerspace">
        <div class="leadership-visual" aria-hidden="true">
          <svg class="leadership-icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor">
            <path class="icon-main" d="M14.7 6.3a1 1 0 0 0 0 1.4l1.6 1.6a1 1 0 0 0 1.4 0l3.106-3.105c.32-.322.863-.22.983.218a6 6 0 0 1-8.259 7.057l-7.91 7.91a1 1 0 0 1-2.999-3l7.91-7.91a6 6 0 0 1 7.057-8.259c.438.12.54.662.219.984z" />
            <circle class="icon-accent-fill" cx="5.15" cy="18.85" r="1.05" />
          </svg>
        </div>

        <div class="leadership-content">
          <div class="leadership-meta">
            <p class="eyebrow">Makerspace Club NU</p>
            <span>February 2025 – April 2025</span>
          </div>
          <h2>Founder and President</h2>

          <details class="leadership-details">
            <summary>View details</summary>
            <div class="leadership-details-content">
              <p>
                At Northeastern University's Oakland campus, I co-founded a club to
                promote the newly established makerspaces. The club's purpose was to
                raise student awareness of the available resources and encourage
                students from all majors to explore their creativity. During one
                semester, our team established the club, organized seven events in
                twelve weeks, and received an award for hosting the best club event
                of the year, as voted on by the Student Involvement staff.
              </p>
              <ul>
                <li>
                  Hosted events featuring activities created with makerspace equipment
                  such as 3D printers, laser cutters, and vinyl cutters.
                </li>
                <li>
                  Coordinated communication with club advisors, sponsors, executive
                  board members, and general club members.
                </li>
                <li>
                  Received recognition for hosting the best club event of the year,
                  as voted on by the Student Involvement staff.
                </li>
              </ul>
            </div>
          </details>
        </div>
      </article>

      <article class="leadership-card leadership-card--mock-trial">
        <div class="leadership-visual" aria-hidden="true">
          <svg class="leadership-icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor">
            <path class="icon-main" d="M12 3v18" />
            <path class="icon-main" d="M5 6h14" />
            <path class="icon-main" d="m5 6-3 7h6L5 6Z" />
            <path class="icon-main" d="m19 6-3 7h6l-3-7Z" />
            <path class="icon-accent" d="M8 21h8" />
          </svg>
        </div>

        <div class="leadership-content">
          <div class="leadership-meta">
            <p class="eyebrow">High School Mock Trial</p>
            <span>2020 – 2024</span>
          </div>
          <h2>Team Captain</h2>

          <details class="leadership-details">
            <summary>View details</summary>
            <div class="leadership-details-content">
              <p>Participated with a team of high school students in mock trial competitions at the distric, regional
                , and state levels. Competitions required months of preparation and were exectued in courtrooms for lawyers
                and judges to observe and critique.
              </p>
              <ul>
                <li>Presented cases to Federal Judges in Mock Court</li>
                <li>State Semifinalist Mock Trial March 2021/24</li>
                <li>State Championship Mock Trial March 2023</li>
              </ul>
            </div>
          </details>
        </div>
      </article>

      <article class="leadership-card leadership-card--football">
        <div class="leadership-visual" aria-hidden="true">
          <svg
  class="leadership-icon"
viewBox="4 4 16 16"
  fill="none"
  stroke="currentColor"
  stroke-linecap="round"
  stroke-linejoin="round"
>
  <ellipse
    class="icon-main"
    cx="12"
    cy="12"
    rx="8.2"
    ry="4.6"
    transform="rotate(-45 12 12)"
    stroke-width="1.8"
  />

  <path
    class="icon-main"
    d="M9.4 14.6 14.6 9.4"
    stroke-width="1.8"
  />

  <path
    class="icon-accent"
    d="m10.2 12.9 1.2 1.2
       M11.5 11.6l1.2 1.2
       M12.8 10.3l1.2 1.2"
    stroke-width="1.8"
  />
</svg>
        </div>

        <div class="leadership-content">
          <div class="leadership-meta">
            <p class="eyebrow">Jesuit Varsity Football</p>
            <span>December 2020 – November 2023</span>
          </div>
          <h2>Team Captain</h2>

          <details class="leadership-details">
            <summary>View details</summary>
            <div class="leadership-details-content">
              <p> Trained and practiced with a varying roster of players in the most competitve High School Football league in Louisiana.</p>
              <ul>
                <li>Led a team of +100 students from 8th – 12th grade, on and off the football field.</li>
                <li>Built better connections with the team than any player in +15 years, as described by the high school’s athletic director.</li>
                <li>Earned multiple awards for academic and athletic achievement, as well as sportsmanship, over +200 athletes.</li>
              </ul>
            </div>
          </details>
        </div>
      </article>

      <article class="leadership-card leadership-card--camp-smile">
        <div class="leadership-visual" aria-hidden="true">
          <svg class="leadership-icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor">
            <circle class="icon-main" cx="12" cy="12" r="9" />
            <path class="icon-accent" d="M8 14s1.5 2 4 2 4-2 4-2" />
            <circle class="icon-main" cx="9" cy="9" r=".6" />
            <circle class="icon-main" cx="15" cy="9" r=".6" />
          </svg>
        </div>

        <div class="leadership-content">
          <div class="leadership-meta">
            <p class="eyebrow">Camp Smile</p>
            <span>July 2023 – 2026</span>
          </div>
          <h2>Counselor</h2>

          <details class="leadership-details">
            <summary>View details</summary>
            <div class="leadership-details-content">
              <p>The camp is a month-long overnight camp that is divided into four separate weeks based on age group. 
                As a counselor, you are paired with a camper for a week who can have a mental and/or physical disability. 
                It is the counselor's job to guide their camper through daily activities and help them
                 have the best week of their summer.</p>
              <ul>
                <li>Cared for campers from ages 12 to +30 with disabilities such as cerebral palsy, autism, and down syndrome.</li>
                <li>Recognized by staff for exemplary leadership, determination, and compassion.</li>
                <li>Trusted by camp staff to speak about the camp on local news television.</li>
              </ul>
            </div>
          </details>
        </div>
      </article>

      <article class="leadership-card leadership-card--responsibility">
        <div class="leadership-visual" aria-hidden="true">
          <svg class="leadership-icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor">
            <path class="icon-main" d="M3 11.5 12 4l9 7.5" />
            <path class="icon-main" d="M5 10.5V21h14V10.5" />
            <path class="icon-accent" d="M9 21v-6h6v6" />
          </svg>
        </div>

        <div class="leadership-content">
          <div class="leadership-meta">
            <p class="eyebrow">Responsibility House</p>
            <span>November 2023 – 2025</span>
          </div>
          <h2>Organizer and Collector</h2>

          <details class="leadership-details">
            <summary>View details</summary>
            <div class="leadership-details-content">
              <p> A charity dedicated to housing the homeless; however, when they are housed, sometimes they lack 
                furniture, bedding, and various other household ammenities and/or supplies. My work for the charity 
                has been to obtain household items and furniture donations to give to people housed or serviced by the charity.</p>
              <ul>
                <li>Organized and ran a household item collection drive for local charity.</li>
                <li>Assisted in collecting furniture, bedding, and housing items from Tulane college students to donate to newly housed people; collected over $40,000 in items.</li>
                <li>Delivered all donations across the city of New Orleans and surrounding areas to people in need.</li>
              </ul>
            </div>
          </details>
        </div>
      </article>

    </div>
  </section>

</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .engineering-interests-heading {
    margin-bottom: 30px;
  }
.interest-grid {
  align-items: start;
}
  /* Engineering Interests dropdown behavior */
  .interest-summary {
    cursor: pointer;
    list-style: none;
  }

  .interest-summary::-webkit-details-marker {
    display: none;
  }

  .interest-summary::marker {
    content: "";
  }

  .interest-chevron {
    display: block;
    width: 18px;
    height: 18px;
    margin: 24px 8px 0 auto;
    border-right: 4px solid rgba(74, 174, 255, 0.95);
    border-bottom: 4px solid rgba(74, 174, 255, 0.95);
    transform: rotate(45deg);
    transition: transform 0.2s ease;
  }

  .interest-card[open] .interest-chevron {
    transform: rotate(225deg);
  }

  .interest-expanded {
    margin-top: 28px;
    padding-top: 28px;
    border-top: 1px solid rgba(74, 174, 255, 0.25);
  }

  .interest-card {
    min-height: 300px;
    padding: 28px;
  }

  .interest-card .capability-card-heading {
    margin-bottom: 28px;
  }

  .interest-card h3 {
    margin: 0;
    color: #ffffff;
    font-size: 1.75rem;
    line-height: 1.25;
    text-transform: none;
  }

  .interest-card p {
    margin: 0;
    color: #ced9e5;
    font-size: 1.35rem;
    line-height: 1.65;
  }

.interest-icon {
  flex: 0 0 98px;
  width: 98px;
  height: 98px;
  border: 3px solid rgba(74, 174, 255, 0.9);
  border-radius: 50%;
}

.interest-icon svg {
  width: 70px;
  height: 70px;
}

  @media (max-width: 540px) {
    .interest-card {
      min-height: auto;
      padding: 24px;
    }
  }


  /* =========================================================
     ABOUT — LEADERSHIP AND SERVICE
     Mirrors the Experience-page card layout.
     ========================================================= */

  .leadership-service-heading {
    margin-bottom: 30px;
  }

  .leadership-list {
    --leadership-gap: 24px;
    --leadership-panel-height: 140px;
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--leadership-gap);
  }

  .leadership-card {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 96px minmax(0, 1fr);
    align-items: start;
    gap: 16px;
  }

  .leadership-visual {
    display: grid;
    height: var(--leadership-panel-height);
    place-items: center;
    padding: 18px 16px;
    overflow: hidden;
    border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.12);
    border-radius: 12px;
    background: linear-gradient(145deg, var(--panel-start), var(--panel-end));
    box-shadow:
      0 12px 26px rgba(8, 31, 57, 0.16),
      0 3px 8px rgba(8, 31, 57, 0.08);
    transition:
      transform 180ms ease,
      box-shadow 180ms ease;
  }

  .leadership-icon {
    width: 56px;
    height: 56px;
    overflow: visible;
  }

  .leadership-icon path,
  .leadership-icon circle {
    fill: none;
    stroke-width: 1.8;
    stroke-linecap: round;
    stroke-linejoin: round;
  }

  .leadership-icon .icon-main {
    stroke: #ffffff;
  }

  .leadership-icon .icon-accent {
    stroke: var(--icon-accent);
  }

  .leadership-icon .icon-accent-fill {
    fill: var(--icon-accent);
    stroke: none;
  }

  .leadership-content {
    min-width: 0;
    min-height: var(--leadership-panel-height);
    padding: 18px 24px;
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 12px;
    background: var(--surface);
    box-shadow:
      0 12px 28px rgba(8, 31, 57, 0.11),
      0 3px 8px rgba(8, 31, 57, 0.05);
    transition:
      transform 180ms ease,
      border-color 180ms ease,
      box-shadow 180ms ease;
  }

  .leadership-card:hover .leadership-visual,
  .leadership-card:hover .leadership-content {
    transform: translateY(-2px);
  }

  .leadership-card:hover .leadership-content {
    border-color: rgba(31, 95, 174, 0.58);
    box-shadow:
      0 18px 38px rgba(8, 31, 57, 0.15),
      0 5px 12px rgba(8, 31, 57, 0.07);
  }

  .leadership-meta {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 18px;
    margin-bottom: 6px;
  }

  .leadership-meta .eyebrow {
    margin-bottom: 0;
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    line-height: 1.4;
  }

  .leadership-meta span {
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    white-space: nowrap;
  }

  .leadership-content h2 {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: 1.55rem;
    line-height: 1.2;
  }

  .leadership-details {
    margin-top: 12px;
    padding-top: 10px;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
  }

  .leadership-details summary {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 20px;
    color: var(--accent);
    font-size: 1rem;
    font-weight: 820;
    cursor: pointer;
    list-style: none;
  }

  .leadership-details summary::-webkit-details-marker {
    display: none;
  }

  .leadership-details summary::after {
    content: "";
    width: 30px;
    height: 30px;
    flex: 0 0 30px;
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 50%;
    background:
      linear-gradient(var(--accent), var(--accent)) center / 12px 3px no-repeat,
      linear-gradient(var(--accent), var(--accent)) center / 3px 12px no-repeat;
  }

  .leadership-details[open] summary::after {
    background:
      linear-gradient(var(--accent), var(--accent)) center / 12px 2px no-repeat;
  }

  .leadership-details-content {
    padding-top: 16px;
    font-size: 1.1rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  .leadership-details-content p {
    text-align: justify;
  }

  .leadership-details-content > :first-child {
    margin-top: 0;
  }

  .leadership-details-content > :last-child {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  .leadership-card--makerspace {
    --panel-start: #12489f;
    --panel-end: #2371dd;
    --icon-accent: #ffd166;
  }

  .leadership-card--mock-trial {
    --panel-start: #17355f;
    --panel-end: #285c9f;
    --icon-accent: #8fd8ff;
  }

  .leadership-card--football {
    --panel-start: #0f3567;
    --panel-end: #1b579d;
    --icon-accent: #8fe3ff;
  }

  .leadership-card--camp-smile {
    --panel-start: #183d73;
    --panel-end: #2f6fb3;
    --icon-accent: #9edcff;
  }

  .leadership-card--responsibility {
    --panel-start: #24396d;
    --panel-end: #385a9d;
    --icon-accent: #9edcff;
  }

  @media (max-width: 760px) {
    .leadership-card {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }

    .leadership-visual {
      height: 104px;
      padding: 18px;
    }

    .leadership-icon {
      width: 64px;
      height: 64px;
    }

    .leadership-content {
      min-height: 0;
      padding: 24px;
    }

    .leadership-meta {
      align-items: flex-start;
      flex-direction: column;
    }

    .leadership-card:hover .leadership-visual,
    .leadership-card:hover .leadership-content {
      transform: none;
    }
  }

</style>
